# Harried Dronesmith: the trigger is "at the beginning of combat on your turn". Turn 1 Bot1 casts it (Black Lotus and a
# Mountain) and makes the first Thopter, which is gone by turn 2. On Bot2's turn 2 there is no Thopter (the combat's
# beginning is not Bot1's turn), and at the beginning of combat on Bot1's turn 3 a new Thopter is made, and sacrificed
# again at that turn's end step.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Harried Dronesmith
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Harried Dronesmith.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Harried Dronesmith; Mountain; Mountain
